#
# v0.10.0 adds the optional `appearance.artifacts` family for non-CSS consumers
# to the generation manifest (consumer + path + format; format is rasi|conf|theme
# and CSS stays exclusively in `targets`). The three appearance schemas are the
# canonical set for this class: `appearance-manifest` (the v2 TOML/JSON manifest
# envelope with the optional root `host` policy), `appearance-json` (the resolved
# tokens.json document; mode and host values already applied) and
# `appearance-artifact` (appearance.json metadata). The generation manifest
# schema is vendored for contract-byte parity; this class emits skin/appearance
# documents, not generations, and never writes an artifact path. The three
# frozen v1 skin schemas are vendored at the same tag for provenance; this class
# no longer emits v1 manifests. All lengths are unitless JSON numbers rendered
# as CSS px, letter-spacing renders as em and font-weight stays unitless.
